comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-30T05:40:13.345Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict-read all-status corpus returned all 2842 items with zero unreadable records. Exact keyword phrase searches across all statuses found none of the three GHSA identifiers. Full closed brace-expansion and prior Scorecard-29 records and histories were read; their different advisory fixes remain valid. This is new advisory exposure in the same package and scanner lineage. The patched release is older than seven days, so no policy exception or paid capability is needed."
  "2026-09-30T05:55:41.282Z","harness:codex","Security contract red phase: real installed minimatch 10.2.6 reaches brace-expansion 5.0.9. Bounded isolated subprocesses reproduce RangeError for 32003-byte parsing-post input and 6403-byte nested-single input; ordinary range/nesting/escaping/nobrace and rewrite controls pass. A separate 16006-byte rewrite finishes in 2289ms. Full dependency audit exits 1 with two high and one moderate advisory; production audit exits 0 with zero findings. Registry patch 5.0.12 was published September 14 and needs no seven-day cooldown exception. Only the existing override floor and its lock resolution change."
  "2026-09-30T05:57:26.397Z","harness:codex","Focused green: frozen-lockfile installation exits 0; all-scope and production audits exit 0 with zero vulnerabilities. Same real public minimatch/brace-expansion subprocess cases on Node 26.9.0 and 5.0.12 all exit 0: parsing-post 33ms; nested members 363ms; nested single 309ms; large-array 85ms; rewrite 27ms versus 2289ms before. Five legitimate controls remain exact. Security caps intentionally retain pathological nesting/rewrite tails as literal input instead of crashing or repeatedly rescanning; normal expansion semantics remain unchanged. Package exports, max/maxLength options and Node engines are retained; maxDepth/maxRewrites are additive. Only the same-major package and integrity resolution changed; no additional dependency upgrades."
  "2026-09-30T06:25:03.596Z","harness:codex",Full validation completed with 9433 passes and one provenance-fixture failure; no coverage report was emitted and exit 3 is not a passing result. Pause security closure while the existing fixture-isolation owner is actively repaired. Initial static check also correctly rejects the newly recorded unregistered recurrence pair; the existing scanner family will be updated after the runner is finished.
  "2026-09-30T07:08:21.795Z","harness:codex","Full verification: Node 26.9.0 coverage exits 0, 9434 tests pass plus two Windows-only skips (1124.00s); all 758 maintained-source modules have exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with zero uncovered counts. pnpm quality:static exits 0 with the existing performance limits and recurrence evidence enforced. Policy tests pass 22/22; positive defect evidence returns ok=true with all 158 recorded recurrence items covered, while the unchanged seeded negative control returns ok=false/exit 1. The independent patch review checked 5483 representative short inputs and 88 max/maxLength combinations with no compatibility mismatch; this is bounded evidence, not whole-library proof. Full audit now includes development dependencies in the scanner family. Alert 29 still reflects the old main tree; do not dismiss it or claim merged-main retirement before its native push scan completes. Required source remediation is implemented; hosted review/merge/Scorecard and publication remain separate states."
